    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Question\n\nI'm wondering if there is a way to make the way that a modified file show more obviously than a `[+]` at the end of the filename. I was thinking something along the lines of a ❌ icon and a checkmark ✅ if the file is saved. Would there be any tips on how to do this?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.statusline</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm wondering if there is a way to make the way that a modified file show more obviously than a <code class=\"notranslate\">[+]</code> at the end of the filename. I was thinking something along the lines of a ❌ icon and a checkmark ✅ if the file is saved. Would there be any tips on how to do this?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.statusline\nQuestion\nI'm wondering if there is a way to make the way that a modified file show more obviously than a [+] at the end of the filename. I was thinking something along the lines of a ❌ icon and a checkmark ✅ if the file is saved. Would there be any tips on how to do this?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
